@startuml device
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans SC"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #6B5FA0
skinparam TitleFontColor #4A2C8F
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 28
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #3AA9B8
  BackgroundColor #E2F6F8
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam card {
  BorderColor #8E6CCF
  BackgroundColor #F8F5FD
}
<style>
card {
  MinimumWidth 210
  HorizontalAlignment center
}
rectangle {
  MinimumWidth 260
}
</style>
title How the call device is chosen\n(workload instantiation places tensors by the same rule)

card "A tensor declaring device: cpu stays on the CPU\nand takes no part below" as pre
card "Any call-time input?" as c1
card "device parameter not None?" as c2
card "Any construction-time tensor?" as c3
card "The current CUDA device;\nNone without CUDA" as r5 #E2F6F8;line:3AA9B8

rectangle "Their device; they must share one" as r1
rectangle "device; a string is parsed\nby torch.device" as r2
rectangle "Their device; several must share one" as r3

pre -down-> c1
c1 -down-> c2 : no
c2 -down-> c3 : no
c3 -down-> r5 : no
c1 -right-> r1 : yes
c2 -right-> r2 : yes
c3 -right-> r3 : yes

r1 -[hidden]down- r2
r2 -[hidden]down- r3

note bottom of r5 #FBFAFE
  Once the call device is chosen, out and the outputs
  are checked or allocated on it; construction-time tensors
  are copied to it and cast to their signature dtype
end note
@enduml
